**New evidence**
Most of the usable 2022 material is campaign-level rather than direct personal-asset evidence. The strongest direct pieces are Trọng’s own anti-corruption and self-critical speeches; the strongest contrary pieces are Reuters and Le Monde on the campaign’s side effects and possible political uses.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Kết luận của Tổng Bí thư Nguyễn Phú Trọng tại Phiên họp thứ 21 của Ban Chỉ đạo Trung ương về phòng, chống tham nhũng, tiêu cực","publisher":"Báo Điện tử Chính phủ","publication_date":"2022-01-20","url":"https://baochinhphu.vn/ket-luan-cua-tong-bi-thu-nguyen-phu-trong-tai-phien-hop-thu-21-cua-ban-chi-dao-trung-uong-ve-phong-chong-tham-nhung-tieu-cuc-10222012020244664.htm","claim":"Trọng said 2022 anti-corruption work should focus on institutional fixes that prevent corruption and on stronger asset-and-income control, especially in corruption-prone sectors.","locator":"lines 193-197","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct government transcript of his own meeting conclusions; strong for what he said and ordered, not for proving his personal honesty.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct. Trọng chaired the meeting and issued the guidance himself, though the claim is about policy posture rather than personal assets.","contrary_evidence":["This is self-issued guidance, not independent proof of his own integrity.","It demonstrates anti-corruption intent, not clean personal hands."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Toàn văn phát biểu của Tổng Bí thư Nguyễn Phú Trọng chúc tết lãnh đạo và nguyên lãnh đạo Đảng, Nhà nước, Mặt trận tổ quốc","publisher":"Ban Nội chính Trung ương","publication_date":"2022-01-30","url":"https://noichinh.vn/tin-tuc-su-kien/tin-trung-uong/202201/toan-van-phat-bieu-cua-tong-bi-thu-nguyen-phu-trong-chuc-tet-lanh-dao-va-nguyen-lanh-dao-dang-nha-nuoc-mat-tran-to-quoc-310626/","claim":"In his New Year address, Trọng said 2022 should prioritize macroeconomic stability, social security, people’s welfare, and a scientific, objective assessment of achievements and shortcomings.","locator":"lines 70-76 and 134-135","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct transcript from a party archive site; strong evidence of stated priorities and self-assessment, but still self-presentation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct statement by Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["This is programmatic rhetoric, not implementation evidence.","It shows stated concern for correction, not proven honesty across all matters."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vacuums, loopholes must be filled in to prevent corruption: Party leader","publisher":"VietnamPlus","publication_date":"2022-06-30","url":"https://en.vietnamplus.vn/vacuums-loopholes-must-be-filled-in-to-prevent-corruption-party-leader-post231946.vnp","claim":"Trọng said shortcomings and loopholes must be filled to prevent corruption and that anti-corruption needs proactive detection and timely, stringent settlement.","locator":"lines 20-23","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"State-linked media reporting a direct speech with clear attribution and quote-like detail; credible for the statement itself, not for proving personal virtue.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct, since the article reports his own speech as party leader and anti-corruption chief.","contrary_evidence":["The speech is still a call to action rather than evidence of personal honesty.","It does not show whether he personally tolerated or concealed misconduct."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Party chief chairs anti-corruption meeting","publisher":"VGP / Government News","publication_date":"2022-08-17","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/party-chief-chairs-anti-corruption-meeting-111220817162948058.htm","claim":"At the 22nd anti-corruption meeting, Trọng said mechanisms must control assets and incomes and that loopholes in bidding, auction, financial management, land use, and public property must be reviewed and amended.","locator":"lines 163-169","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government transcript with specific policy instructions and meeting context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct. He chaired the meeting and gave the instruction as party chief.","contrary_evidence":["This is institutional anti-corruption steering, not proof of his own clean finances.","The article reflects policy direction rather than independent scrutiny of the ruler."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Party chief orders more drastic actions against corruption","publisher":"VietnamPlus","publication_date":"2022-11-18","url":"https://en.vietnamplus.vn/party-chief-orders-more-drastic-actions-against-corruption-post244113.vnp","claim":"Trọng ordered that corruption violations be punished strictly without any forbidden zone or exception, including for fugitives abroad, and pushed faster investigation, prosecution, trial, and asset recovery.","locator":"lines 20-29","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"State-media report on a direct public order with concrete investigative and recovery measures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct, because the article attributes the order to Trọng as head of the steering committee.","contrary_evidence":["Aggressive anti-corruption enforcement can still serve factional or political aims.","The piece shows scope and severity of enforcement, not the ruler’s own asset disclosures."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Phát biểu của Tổng Bí thư Nguyễn Phú Trọng tại Hội nghị Quân chính toàn quân năm 2022","publisher":"Báo Điện tử Chính phủ","publication_date":"2022-12-20","url":"https://baochinhphu.vn/phat-bieu-cua-tong-bi-thu-nguyen-phu-trong-tai-hoi-nghi-quan-chinh-toan-quan-nam-2022-102221220183023839.htm","claim":"Trọng acknowledged shortcomings in the armed forces, including that some officers failed to set an example, discipline was weak, and some serious incidents were detected and handled too slowly.","locator":"lines 223-225","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official transcript with explicit self-critical language and concrete criticisms.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct. This is Trọng speaking to the military hierarchy under his party authority.","contrary_evidence":["The criticism concerns an institution under his authority, not his personal private conduct.","It shows candor about institutional failure, not direct evidence of personal self-dealing."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Analysis: Vietnam's anti-graft crackdown chills supply chains, investment","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-28","url":"https://m.investing.com/news/commodities-news/analysis-vietnams-antigraft-crackdown-chills-supply-chains-investment-2952525?ampMode=1","claim":"Reuters reported that Vietnam's anti-corruption drive had paralyzed many routine transactions, caused shortages of essential goods, and left about 65% of large hospitals short of drugs and medical products.","locator":"lines 10-14","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with direct market and hospital impact claims, though still an analysis relying partly on official and third-party sources.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. The report concerns the campaign led by Trọng, but it does not prove his own deceit or enrichment.","contrary_evidence":["The story describes harmful side effects of enforcement, not personal corruption by Trọng.","It can also be read as evidence of an anti-graft effort with real bite."],"lenses":["7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"27 senior Party members disciplined in H1/2022","publisher":"Vietnamnet","publication_date":"2022-08-18","url":"https://vietnamnet.vn/en/27-senior-party-members-disciplined-in-h1-2022-2050847.html","claim":"Vietnamnet reported that 295 Party members were disciplined in the first six months of 2022, including 27 officials managed by the Politburo and Secretariat, and that inspectors proposed recovering VND 15.41 trillion.","locator":"lines 52-65","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"State-linked media reporting concrete disciplinary statistics and recovery proposals from the anti-corruption meeting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but meaningful. The disciplinary action occurred under Trọng’s anti-corruption leadership, but it does not by itself show personal wrongdoing or personal honesty.","contrary_evidence":["The data show system-level discipline, not Trọng’s own assets or disclosures.","Such figures can reflect political control as well as integrity enforcement."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam’s anti-corruption drive strengthens nation, not internal power struggles, party leader","publisher":"VietnamNews","publication_date":"2022-11-19","url":"https://vietnamnews.vn/politics-laws/1397057/anti-corruption-drive-strengthens-nation-not-internal-power-struggles-party-leader.html","claim":"Trọng rejected claims that the anti-corruption drive was an internal power struggle and said a stronger anti-corruption drive makes the Party and public trust stronger.","locator":"search-result snippet and headline summary","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"State-media snippet is useful for the statement itself, but the page was blocked on open and the item is largely self-justifying.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct statement by Trọng, but it is self-defensive and not independently verified.","contrary_evidence":["The claim is self-justifying and contested by outside analysts.","The blocked page limited independent line-by-line verification."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vietnam arrests former coast guard chief over 'embezzlement' case","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-04-18","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/vietnam-arrests-former-coast-guard-123023499.html","claim":"Reuters reported that Vietnam’s defense ministry detained a former coast guard commander and six other senior officers on suspicion of embezzlement as the party intensified its graft crackdown.","locator":"Reuters snippet in search result","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire report is strong for the arrest and campaign context, but it remains campaign-level evidence rather than a direct record of Trọng’s private conduct.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. The case unfolded under the party-led campaign associated with Trọng, but it does not show his own assets, family ties, or false statements.","contrary_evidence":["This is evidence of enforcement against a senior security official, not evidence of Trọng’s own corruption.","It may equally support a clean-up narrative or a political purge narrative."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"In Vietnam, the anti-corruption fight is in full swing","publisher":"Le Monde","publication_date":"2022-06-28","url":"https://www.lemonde.fr/en/economy/article/2022/06/28/in-vietnam-the-anti-corruption-fight-is-in-full-swing_5988162_19.html","claim":"Le Monde reported that the anti-corruption campaign initiated by Trọng also served a political function by bringing challengers and potential rivals into line.","locator":"search-result snippet and summary lines about the campaign’s political function","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Reputable international newspaper analysis, but interpretive and not a finding about Trọng’s personal assets or lies.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly about the 2022 campaign context.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect. The campaign is associated with Trọng, but the article is analysis rather than direct evidence of personal deception.","contrary_evidence":["The claim is interpretive and may overstate factional motive.","It does not show personal enrichment or a specific hidden conflict of interest."],"lenses":["7B.7","7B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I looked across roughly 25-40 documents, then kept the ones that best met the personal-nexus filter for 7B. The retained set is concentrated in direct Trọng speeches and orders, plus a few Reuters/Le Monde pieces on the campaign’s effects and possible political use.

I rejected or de-prioritized:
- Pure country-level corruption indicators such as WGI, V-Dem, and CPI, because they do not show Trọng’s personal honesty or benefit.
- Broad repression and censorship reporting that was relevant to 3B/4B but did not establish a direct integrity nexus.
- Generic profiles and background articles that only repeated his title or biography.
- Older explainers from 2018 and 2021 unless they were useful background for the 2022 office context.
- Later 2024-2026 articles on the campaign’s aftermath, because they were outside the target year.
- Duplicate state-media reports that repeated the same anti-corruption meeting figures without adding a distinct claim.
- One VietnamNews page that was blocked on open; I relied only on its search snippet and treated it as context, not as strong independent proof.

**Remaining gaps**
- There is still no strong direct evidence on Trọng’s own assets, family finances, gifts, or private conflicts of interest in 2022.
- I did not find verified allegations or findings tying him personally to embezzlement, undisclosed wealth, or nepotistic enrichment.
- The best evidence is mostly about his anti-corruption posture and the campaign he led, not his private integrity record.
- More search would help only if you want a deeper probe into asset declarations, family/business links, or any independent investigative records that mention him by name.
